@flexiarg math-formalization-CA/complex-arg-of-cpow-root
@title Principal Argument of a Complex Power Root
@sigils [🌀/角]
@keywords arg, cpow, slitPlane, argument, principal-root, wedge, MapsTo
@audience lean-provers, complex-analysis
@tone heuristic
@difficulty moderate
@subjects complex-analysis
@instantiates math-informal-CA/estimate-by-bounding
@examples a01A12

! conclusion:
  Control arg of a principal n-th root by proving arg divides by n, built from
  arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I rather than searched for as a Mathlib lemma.

  + IF: Goal needs |(x ^ (1/n : ℂ)).arg| < bound, or x ^ (1/n : ℂ) ∈ slitPlane.

  + HOWEVER: Mathlib has no direct `arg_cpow` division lemma as of this writing.

  + THEN: Rewrite (1/n : ℂ) = ((1/n : ℝ) : ℂ) by norm_num, apply Complex.cpow_ofReal,
    then convert Complex.arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I (rpow positivity) with
    x.arg / n ∈ Set.Ioc (-Real.pi) Real.pi from Complex.neg_pi_lt_arg and
    Complex.arg_le_pi plus linarith. Pair with Complex.arg_lt_pi_iff /
    Complex.arg_eq_zero_iff for slitPlane / real-axis exclusion.
    + LEAN:
      api[Complex.cpow_ofReal] api[Complex.arg_mul_cos_add_sin_mul_I]
      api[Complex.arg_lt_pi_iff] api[Complex.arg_eq_zero_iff]
      tactic[norm_num → linarith → convert]

  + BECAUSE: The polar form lemma already fixes the argument once the exponent
    is manifestly real and the half-open angle interval is supplied.
